From 10ddba2a95afae1661c5000b8444e7f200571a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 19:55:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 587/638] aros: --aros-spoof-platform=linux|windows

Present the browser as that OS in the User-Agent string (reduced and
full forms), the UA client hints (Sec-CH-UA-Platform/-Platform-Version,
navigator.userAgentData) and navigator.platform.  Sites that gate
features on an OS allow-list never try on "AROS"; the switch lets such
pages be exercised before they know about us.  Off by default; the
switch is propagated to renderers since navigator.platform is minted
there.
---
